//RS /// The one raise door for a cancel, so the cleanup rule holds for every caller —
//RS /// wait points, the crypto/HTTP host seams that take this function as a pointer,
//RS /// and the JIT. While an unwind is in flight this returns instead of raising:
//RS /// the cancel stays recorded on `JetTaskControl.cancelled` and lands on that
//RS /// unwind's outcome, because a second raise from drop glue aborts the process
//RS /// (#2007) rather than cancelling anything.
